WHY NO DERIVATIVES: a conformance standard whose text can be silently
altered certifies nothing. "Conforms to KNP-26" has to mean one document.
Read the standards, cite them, run their verifiers against your own record,
publish your verdict, disagree with them in your own words under your own
name — all fine, none of it needs this permission. What ND forbids is
shipping an edited KNP that still calls itself KNP.

NOT A TRADEMARK LICENSE: nothing here grants rights in the names
Retro-Prescient Audit, The Prescient Desk, NebelKrähe, Kaos Kontrol,
