Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, this software is
distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY
KIND, either express or implied.

WHY PERMISSIVE: the moat was never the code. The whole thesis of this desk
is "don't trust the builder — run the verifier," and a verifier a stranger
cannot take, read, modify, and run against the desk's own published files is
not a verifier, it is a press release. Fork the instruments. Point them at
this desk first.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
IF THE TWO PARTS DISAGREE ABOUT A FILE
Runnable code is Part B. Everything else is Part A. Where a file is both
(an HTML page carrying an inline script), the prose is Part A and the script
is Part B.

WHAT NEITHER PART GRANTS OR RESTRICTS
The methods themselves. Sealing a forecast before its outcome, scoring it
misfire-inclusive, and publishing a verifier are not this desk's property
and this license does not pretend otherwise — KNM 7.04 already said so in
the standard's own voice. Copyright here covers these expressions of the
method, not the practice of it. Go audit something.

